"""Tests of Xvnc: the server is started on a display of its own, X programs
are run on it, and it is driven over both of its protocols.

    run-tests [options] [name...]

    --xvnc PATH       the server to test (default: the one built in this tree)
    --failures FILE   write the names of the failed tests there, one a line;
                      the exit status is then 0 if the tests could be run
    --list            list the tests
    --keep            keep each test's directory (logs) under tests/out
    -v                show what the servers print

A test that needs a program this machine lacks (xterm, xclock, xmessage,
xwininfo, a window manager, xpra) is skipped, which is not a failure.
"""

